          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let’s Play a Game #1"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.35,
            0.885,
            0.418
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This is an angle guessing game! Play this game with your classmates by making two teams, Team 1 and Team 2. Here are the instructions and rules for the game:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.428,
            0.885,
            0.496
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Team 1",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " secretly choose an angle measure, for example, 49° and makes an angle with that measure using a protractor without Team 2 being able to see it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.199,
            0.502,
            0.885,
            0.57
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Team 2",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " now gets to look at the angle. They have to quickly discuss and guess the number of degrees in the angle (without using a protractor!)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.576,
            0.884,
            0.62
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Team 1",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " now demonstrates the true measure of the angle with a protractor."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.628,
            0.885,
            0.718
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Team 2 scores the number of points that is the absolute difference in degrees between their guess and the correct measure. For example, if Team 2 guesses 39°, then they score 10 points (49°–39°)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.199,
            0.724,
            0.884,
            0.768
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Each team gets five turns. The winner is the team with the lowest score!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.788,
            0.436,
            0.811
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let’s Play a Game #2"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.817,
            0.885,
            0.886
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We now change the rules of the game a bit. Play this game with your classmates by again making two teams, Team 1 and Team 2. Here are the instructions and rules:"
            }
          ]
        },
